    "https://brocku.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/brocku_careers/job/St-Catharines-Main-Campus/Technical-Analyst--Level-1_JR-1025328": {
      "title": "Technical Analyst, Level 1",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nBrock University is located on the traditional territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabe peoples, many of whom continue to live and work here today. This territory is covered by the Upper Canada Treaties and is within the land protected by the Dish with One Spoon Wampum Agreement.  We are one of Canada’s outstanding comprehensive universities, where excellence and innovation thrive! Brock has been proudly recognized as a Hamilton-Niagara Top Employer for eight consecutive years. Brock continues to earn recognition as one of Canada’s Best Employers and one of Canada’s Best Employers for Diversity in 2026. For the second consecutive year, Forbes, in partnership with Statista, also named Brock one of Canada’s Top Employers for Company Culture. At Brock, you will find a welcoming, inclusive community and an exciting range of meaningful career opportunities. Ignite new possibilities for your career. Break through at Brock. Post End Date: September 17, 2026 at 11:59 PM This job advertisement is to fill an existing vacancy in the Administrative Professional (Employee Group) Please note: This is a   6-month   fixed-term contract       About the Role:   Reporting to the Interim Director, Client Services   the   Technical   Analyst, Level 1 provides customer service and   technical   support/ assistance   to faculty, staff, and students in   a   timely   and   accurate   manner. The   incumbent will assess technical problems, provide solution s   to technology   problems   and incorporate and adapt   new   technology   and   efficiencies   into the Brock Community.      T he   Technical Analyst, Level 1   will:     Perform analysis, diagnosis,   documentation   and   resolution   of complex IT system problems for clients;    Recommend, implement, and document corrective solutions;     Enforce ITS security policies and promote ITS best practices within the University community;    Work as a team member to collaboratively resolve client incidents and service requests with other team members,   partners   and suppliers;   Record all problems, service requests, change requests, and incidents in the ITS ticketing system including request, solution, and effort;    Communicate effectively with the client throughout the life of a ticket developing strong relationships;    Respond to all assigned tickets in   a timely   and   appropriate manner ;   Create, build, analyze, test, and deploy operating systems and application packages for supported hardware, ensuring all configurations meet IT standards;    Utilize system management tools to inventory, monitor, patch, and update supported software,   systems   and servers;    Provide basic technical support for enterprise software packages (such as Brock Card, Residence systems, scheduling software, email, and print accounting) including updates to applications and corresponding systems and servers, handing off to Technical Analysts, Level 3   when higher level technical support is required ;    Provide IT specialist support and accountability, including troubleshooting, setup, implementation, upgrades, research, and documentation;    Liaise between clients and other ITS teams to resolve issues and create efficiencies;    Provide local and remote technical support to faculty,   staff   and students;    Maintain an inventory of Brock University client owned equipment for asset management and repair.       Key   S kills and   Experience :   Three-year   college diploma or university degree in a related field;    Technical support experience in a help desk   environment ;    Knowledge of   the   help desk environment,   requirements   and responsibilities;    Knowledge of computer hardware and software, systems and configuration management, active directory, software installation, and Microsoft Exchange;     Working knowledge of the interactions between computer software, hardware,   servers   and networks;    Knowledge of ITIL principles;     Knowledge of MS-Windows, Apple, and Linux Operating systems;     Knowledge of various software programs ,   business   applications   and internet browsers ;    Working knowledge of anti-virus systems;    Working knowledge of mobile devices including setup and configuration;   Strong verbal and interpersonal communication skills   with the ability to interact with irate or upset clients ;   Self-motivated and directed, with the demonstrated ability to multitask and effectively manage multiple and competing deadlines,   service   and incident requests;    Strong troubleshooting capabilities and the ability to provide   appropriate solutions , knowing when to hand off higher-level technical support requirements .      Preferred or Asset Skill s:    Experience working in an educational or government organization;    ITIL Foundation certification;    Microsoft Certification;    Apple Certification.     Salary   and   Total Rewards:    Job Grade   J , Salary Scale ( $ 57,267-$91,627 );   Target Hiring   Salary: $57,267     This position is   required   to work on campus five (5) days per week.    * The final salary is based on   experien ce, internal equity, and budget considerations within the target hiring range. We are committed to offering flexible work arrangements where possible as outlined in our Flexible Work Arrangement Policy . As a student-centered organization, all employees are required to work on campus as needed.   Brock University is committed to creating a respectful and equitable workplace. We strive to foster a culture of diversity and inclusion in our work and learning environments. We welcome applications from all qualified individuals and actively encourage applications from women, people with disabilities, members of the 2SLGBTQIA+ community, Indigenous Peoples, people who identify as Black, African and/or Caribbean, as racialized and/or as from ethnic and cultural minority groups, and other underrepresented demographic groups at Brock and in the Niagara region. Brock also recognizes intersectionality and the interconnected identities, histories, and experiences of these aforementioned groups .   We are committed to inclusive and barrier-free recruitment, and we accommodat e the needs of applicants throughout all stages of the recruitment process, as outlined in our Employment Accommodation Policy and consistent with the requirements of the Ontario Human Rights Code . Please contact talent@brocku.ca   if you require a disability related accommodation so we can ensure you r participation needs are met.   Brock University does not use AI Technology at any stage of the recruitment process.   We appreciate all applications received . C andidates that are selected for an interview will be contacted.   Learn more about Brock University by visiting www.brocku.ca ."
