    "https://brocku.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/brocku_careers/job/St-Catharines-Main-Campus/Learning-Services-Operations-Coordinator_JR-1025325": {
      "title": "Learning Services Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nBrock University is located on the traditional territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabe peoples, many of whom continue to live and work here today. This territory is covered by the Upper Canada Treaties and is within the land protected by the Dish with One Spoon Wampum Agreement.  We are one of Canada’s outstanding comprehensive universities, where excellence and innovation thrive! Brock has been proudly recognized as a Hamilton-Niagara Top Employer for eight consecutive years. Brock continues to earn recognition as one of Canada’s Best Employers and one of Canada’s Best Employers for Diversity in 2026. For the second consecutive year, Forbes, in partnership with Statista, also named Brock one of Canada’s Top Employers for Company Culture. At Brock, you will find a welcoming, inclusive community and an exciting range of meaningful career opportunities. Ignite new possibilities for your career. Break through at Brock. Post End Date: September 23, 2026 at 11:59 PM This job advertisement is to fill an existing vacancy in the Administrative Professional (Employee Group) About the Role:   Reporting to the Associate Director, the Learning Services Operations Coordinator plays a critical role in ensuring the effective delivery of Brock's academic support services. The   Learning Services Operations   Coordinator oversees operational processes that support tutoring, peer learning initiatives, academic integrity programming, non-credit learning opportunities, and other student success programs.     The successful candidate will coordinate departmental operations, support   financial management   and resource planning, lead data collection and reporting activities, and develop communications strategies to promote student engagement. The role also provides support to student staff and serves as a key resource in ensuring Learning Services programs   operate   efficiently and effectively.     T he   Learning   Services   Operations Coordinator   will:     Coordinate the scheduling,   logistics , and operational resources   required   for the successful delivery of Learning Services programs and services.   Manage operational systems supporting registrations, appointments, program administration, and service delivery.   Coordinate campus space bookings and resource allocation for workshops, events, and learning support initiatives.   Support the day-to-day operations of Learning Services to ensure an efficient, student-centered experience.   Monitor budgets, expenditures, revenues, and financial records, ensuring compliance with university policies and procedures.   Process payments, reconcile revenues, support payroll activities, and   assist   with financial reporting and resource planning.   Lead the collection, organization, and analysis of program participation, engagement, and outcomes data.   Prepare reports and   provide   data-informed insights to support program evaluation, strategic planning, and decision-making.   Maintain data management processes and support continuous improvement of reporting standards and assessment practices.   Develop and implement marketing, communications, and outreach initiatives to increase awareness and participation in Learning Services programs.   Coordinate digital and print communications, ensuring content is   accurate , accessible, and aligned with institutional branding standards.   Collaborate with campus partners and stakeholders to promote services, support student success initiatives, and strengthen cross-campus engagement.   Assist   with the planning and delivery of departmental projects, events, and initiatives while fostering effective team collaboration.   Support continuous improvement efforts that enhance operational effectiveness, service quality, and   the overall   student experience.     Key   S kills and   Experience :     Undergraduate Degree   or the   equivalent combination of education and experience .   1-2   years' experience   in business , project management, human resources, education   Strong organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills.   Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities and meet competing deadlines.   Excellent verbal and written communication skills.   Strong customer service orientation and commitment to supporting diverse student populations.   Ability to work independently while   maintaining   a collaborative team approach.   Experience collecting, analyzing, and reporting on data to support decision-making.   Strong financial administration and record-keeping skills.   Proficiency   with Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel.   Ability to exercise sound judgment and manage confidential information with professionalism and discretion.   Commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, accessibility, and student success. Preferred or Asset Skill s:    Experience working in student affairs, student services, or academic support environments.   Knowledge of university administrative systems, ticketing platforms, point-of-sale systems, or database management.   Familiarity with marketing, communications, and student engagement strategies. Salary   and   Total Rewards:    Job Grade   J , Salary   Scale   ( $ 57,267-$91,627 );   Target Hiring Range:   $57,267-$62,424 .   T his   is a permanent position that   includes :      Health & Dental Benefits:   Comprehensive extended health, dental, and vision coverage.   Pension Plan:   Enrollment eligibility in the Brock University Pension Plan.   Vacation:   Up to 3 weeks per year, in addition to university holidays.   Professional Development:   Eligibility for the Brock Tuition Waiver Program.   *The final salary is based on experience, internal equity, and budget considerations within the target hiring range. We are committed to offering flexible work arrangements where possible as outlined in our Flexible Work Arrangement Policy . As a student-centered organization, all employees are required to work on campus as needed.   Brock University is committed to creating a respectful and equitable workplace. We strive to foster a culture of diversity and inclusion in our work and learning environments. We welcome applications from all qualified individuals and actively encourage applications from women, people with disabilities, members of the 2SLGBTQIA+ community, Indigenous Peoples, people who identify as Black, African and/or Caribbean, as racialized and/or as from ethnic and cultural minority groups, and other underrepresented demographic groups at Brock and in the Niagara region. Brock also recognizes intersectionality and the interconnected identities, histories, and experiences of these aforementioned groups .   We are committed to inclusive and barrier-free recruitment, and we accommodat e the needs of applicants throughout all stages of the recruitment process, as outlined in our Employment Accommodation Policy and consistent with the requirements of the Ontario Human Rights Code . Please contact talent@brocku.ca   if you require a disability related accommodation so we can ensure you r participation needs are met.   Brock University does not use AI Technology at any stage of the recruitment process.   We appreciate all applications received . C andidates that are selected for an interview will be contacted.   Learn more about Brock University by visiting www.brocku.ca ."
