    "https://brocku.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/brocku_careers/job/St-Catharines-Main-Campus/Nursing-Clinical-Assistant_JR-1025337": {
      "title": "Nursing Clinical Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nBrock University is located on the traditional territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabe peoples, many of whom continue to live and work here today. This territory is covered by the Upper Canada Treaties and is within the land protected by the Dish with One Spoon Wampum Agreement.  We are one of Canada’s outstanding comprehensive universities, where excellence and innovation thrive! Brock has been proudly recognized as a Hamilton-Niagara Top Employer for eight consecutive years. Brock continues to earn recognition as one of Canada’s Best Employers and one of Canada’s Best Employers for Diversity in 2026. For the second consecutive year, Forbes, in partnership with Statista, also named Brock one of Canada’s Top Employers for Company Culture. At Brock, you will find a welcoming, inclusive community and an exciting range of meaningful career opportunities. Ignite new possibilities for your career. Break through at Brock. Post End Date: September 30, 2026 at 11:59 PM This job advertisement is to fill an existing vacancy in the Administrative Professional (Employee Group)   About the Role:     Reporting to   the Manager, Clinical Operations, the Nursing Clinical Assistant   provides administrative coordination for clinical education activities within the Nursing program. The   Nursing Clinical Assistant   supports Clinical Nursing Instructor (CNI) hiring and onboarding, regulatory and preceptor administration, clinical data reporting, and established placement workflows. The incumbent  maintains   accurate  records, quality improvement structures, coordinates routine communications with students and external bodies, and escalates clinical issues, policy, compliance, or placement decisions to the  appropriate program  lead.      T he   Nursing Clinical Assistant   will :       Coordinate the administrative components of CNI recruitment, including interview scheduling, registration verification against established requirements, distribution and   hiring, onboarding , and maintenance of candidate records;    Process approved CNI staffing changes, including absences and call-ins, make-up shifts, replacement assignments, and contract amendments, ensuring information is communicated and recorded accurately;    Coordinate CNI onboarding activities and learning modules, follow up on outstanding requirements, and  maintain  current onboarding records;    Respond to routine CNI questions concerning established administrative processes and direct clinical, employment, policy, or collective agreement matters to the  appropriate resource ;    Administer established student re-entry processes, including coordinating payment information, monitoring completion of required steps, and  maintaining  supporting records;    Maintain  preceptor contact information and coordinate recognition activities ;   Coordinate routine correspondence and doc ument exchange with the   College of Nurses   of Ontario (CNO ) ,  maintain  records of submissi ons and responses, and escalate matters requiring interpretation or professional judgment;    Maintain organized and confidential clinical program records  in accordance with  University requirements and applicable privacy practices ;   Extract and  consolidate  data from clinical-related systems and platforms to support Program Quality Improvement (PQI), operational planning, and reporting requirements;    Review data for completeness and consistency, conduct routine analysis,  identify  trends or discrepancies, and prepare summaries, tables, and reports for program leadership;    Provide administrative support for clinical placement processes as  required , including data entry, document collection, status tracking, scheduling support, and maintenance of placement records;    Monitor shared email accounts and phone lines and respond to routine student inquiries using approved information, templates, and service standards;    Collaborate with Nursing program staff, faculty members, University departments, and external partners to obtain information, resolve routine administrative issues, and support established timelines.      Key   S kills and   Experience :   Diploma or degree in related discipline   and/or   equivalent combination of education and experience ;   Experience in administration or program coordination, preferably in a post-secondary,  healthcare , clinical education, or similarly regulated environment ;   Experience coordinating records, schedules, hiring or onboarding processes, and confidential information ;   Knowledge of administrative practices and the ability to learn University, Nursing program, clinical placement, and regulatory processes;    Proficiency  with office productivity software, spreadsheets, databases, survey tools, and web-based information systems;    Ability to extract, organize,  validate , and analyze data and prepare clear,  accurate  reports and summaries;    Strong attention to detail and ability to  maintain   accurate  records, track requirements, and meet recurring deadlines;    Excellent organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to coordinate multiple concurrent processes;    Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to prepare professional correspondence;    Sound judgment in handling confidential and sensitive information and in recognizing matters that require escalation;    Strong customer-service and interpersonal skills when working with students, instructors, faculty, staff, regulatory bodies, and external partners;    Ability and willingness to learn and adapt to  new technologies , systems, and evolving program processes; and    Promotes and embodies inclusivity and respect within the workplace and the broader community.     Preferred or Asset Skill s:    Experience with clinical education administration, CNO-related processes, data reporting, survey tools, or placement systems is an asset.       Salary   and   Total Rewards:    Job Grade   I , Salary Scale ( $ 52,798- $84,476 );   Target Hiring Range:   $ 52,7 98   –   $ 56 ,000*   T his   is a   permanent   position that   includes :      Health & Dental Benefits:   Comprehensive extended health, dental, and vision coverage.   Pension Plan:   Enrollment eligibility in the Brock University Pension Plan.   Vacation:   Up to 3 weeks per year, in addition to university holidays.   Professional Development:   Eligibility   for the Brock Tuition Waiver Program.   *The final salary is based on experience, internal equity, and budget considerations within the target hiring range.   We are committed to offering flexible work arrangements where possible as outlined in our Flexible Work Arrangement Policy . As a student-centered organization, all employees are required to work on campus as needed.   Brock University is committed to creating a respectful and equitable workplace. We strive to foster a culture of diversity and inclusion in our work and learning environments. We welcome applications from all qualified individuals and actively encourage applications from women, people with disabilities, members of the 2SLGBTQIA+ community, Indigenous Peoples, people who identify as Black, African and/or Caribbean, as racialized and/or as from ethnic and cultural minority groups, and other underrepresented demographic groups at Brock and in the Niagara region. Brock also recognizes intersectionality and the interconnected identities, histories, and experiences of these aforementioned groups .   We are committed to inclusive and barrier-free recruitment, and we accommodat e the needs of applicants throughout all stages of the recruitment process, as outlined in our Employment Accommodation Policy and consistent with the requirements of the Ontario Human Rights Code . Please contact talent@brocku.ca   if you require a disability related accommodation so we can ensure you r participation needs are met.   Brock University does not use AI Technology at any stage of the recruitment process.   We appreciate all applications received . C andidates that are selected for an interview will be contacted.   Learn more about Brock University by visiting www.brocku.ca ."
    },
    "https://brocku.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/brocku_careers/job/St-Catharines-Main-Campus/Graduate-Program-Coordinator--Faculty-of-Social-Science_JR-1025333": {
      "title": "Graduate Program Coordinator, Faculty of Social Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nBrock University is located on the traditional territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabe peoples, many of whom continue to live and work here today. This territory is covered by the Upper Canada Treaties and is within the land protected by the Dish with One Spoon Wampum Agreement.  We are one of Canada’s outstanding comprehensive universities, where excellence and innovation thrive! Brock has been proudly recognized as a Hamilton-Niagara Top Employer for eight consecutive years. Brock continues to earn recognition as one of Canada’s Best Employers and one of Canada’s Best Employers for Diversity in 2026. For the second consecutive year, Forbes, in partnership with Statista, also named Brock one of Canada’s Top Employers for Company Culture. At Brock, you will find a welcoming, inclusive community and an exciting range of meaningful career opportunities. Ignite new possibilities for your career. Break through at Brock. Post End Date: October 1, 2026 at 11:59 PM This job advertisement is to fill an existing vacancy in the Administrative Professional (Employee Group) Please note this is a part-time, ongoing position at 17.5 hours per week. About the Role: Reporting to the Dean’s Office, the Graduate Program Coordinator is responsible for coordinating graduate program operations across recruitment, admissions, academic advising, and program delivery. The role ensures a high-quality student experience while supporting faculty and maintaining compliance with academic policies and standards. The Graduate Program Coordinator will: Coordinate the administrative delivery and operations of graduate programs, including course scheduling, registration support, academic milestone tracking, grade submission, and key academic processes such as comprehensive examinations, thesis proposals, and defenses, while ensuring compliance, data integrity, and adherence to policies and timelines; Facilitate communication between Graduate Program Directors, supervisors/co-supervisors, and students regarding academic requirements, program milestones, timelines, and progression concerns; Coordinate scholarship, funding, fellowship, bursary, and award processes, including applicant support, submission verification, adjudication activities, ranking meetings, and record maintenance; Contribute to program communications and marketing (e.g., website, social media) in collaboration with internal partners, conduct reviews of program webpages to ensure information is accurate, current and aligned with program needs; Support the end-to-end graduate recruitment and admissions lifecycle, including outreach, presentations, information sessions, applicant advising, application intake, and review, to attract qualified candidates and ensure efficient, compliant admissions processes; Organize applicant profiles and summaries, initiate admission decisions based on Graduate Program Committee recommendations, including offers, applicable offer conditions and funding items, waitlists, rejections and application closures; Monitor application and enrolment activity to support admissions planning, waitlist management, Teaching Assistantship opportunities, and admission closures in alignment with program targets; Provide comprehensive academic advising and proactive student support by interpreting and applying academic regulations, resolving routine academic issues, and promoting student progression, engagement, and timely degree completion; Monitor student progression, performance, engagement, and academic milestones; identify risks to completion, implement or escalate interventions, and use student outcomes data to inform advising and program improvements; Support student engagement, retention, and success through the promotion of professional development and experiential opportunities and by connecting students with appropriate academic and support services; and Build and maintain collaborative relationships with faculty, academic leaders, the Faculty of Graduate Studies & Postdoctoral Affairs (FGSPA), and campus partners to coordinate support for students, exchange information, resolve issues. This role may occasionally require work outside regular business hours, including evenings or weekends, based on operational needs. Key Skills and Experience: Knowledge of Faculty of Social Science programs and courses (undergraduate and graduate); Knowledge of academic advising principles, models, and counselling approaches; Understanding of graduate curriculum, course requirements, prerequisites, and scheduling within the Faculty; Awareness and understanding of various collective agreements; Knowledge of privacy legislation (e.g., FIPPA) and the ability to interpret and apply academic policies, regulations, and governance documents. Proficiency with computer systems and software applications; Ability and willingness to learn and adapt to emerging technologies, including AI tools and platforms; Promotes and embodies inclusiveness and respect within the workplace and the broader community; Strong communication and interpersonal skills, including active listening and clear written/verbal communication; Ability to coach, mentor, and motivate students, including identifying risk and making appropriate referrals; Demonstrates empathy, discretion, and professionalism when handling sensitive or confidential situation; Ability to liaise with multiple stakeholders and build effective relationships across the institution; Strong organizational, prioritization, and multitasking skills, with accurate record-keeping practices; and Effective problem-solving skills with the ability to adapt and apply new knowledge quickly. Preferred or Asset Skills: Administrative and academic advising experience within a graduate education setting; Graduate degree; Comprehensive understanding of University/public sector governance, policies, procedures and culture; Experience networking with community partners and partner development; Research grant writing or review experience; and Data collection and quantitative/qualitative analysis experience. Salary and Total Rewards: Job Grade K, Salary Scale ($62,115.00 - 99,384.00); Target Hiring Range: $62,115.00 - $65,000* prorated to reflect part-time hours This is a permanent, part-time position that includes:   Health & Dental Benefits: Comprehensive extended health, dental, and vision coverage. Pension Plan: Enrollment eligibility in the Brock University Pension Plan. Vacation: Up to 3 weeks per year, in addition to university holidays. Professional Development: Eligibility for the Brock Tuition Waiver Program. *The final salary is based on experience, internal equity, and budget considerations within the target hiring range. We are committed to offering flexible work arrangements where possible as outlined in our Flexible Work Arrangement Policy . As a student-centered organization, all employees are required to work on campus as needed.   Brock University is committed to creating a respectful and equitable workplace. We strive to foster a culture of diversity and inclusion in our work and learning environments. We welcome applications from all qualified individuals and actively encourage applications from women, people with disabilities, members of the 2SLGBTQIA+ community, Indigenous Peoples, people who identify as Black, African and/or Caribbean, as racialized and/or as from ethnic and cultural minority groups, and other underrepresented demographic groups at Brock and in the Niagara region. Brock also recognizes intersectionality and the interconnected identities, histories, and experiences of these aforementioned groups .   We are committed to inclusive and barrier-free recruitment, and we accommodat e the needs of applicants throughout all stages of the recruitment process, as outlined in our Employment Accommodation Policy and consistent with the requirements of the Ontario Human Rights Code . Please contact talent@brocku.ca   if you require a disability related accommodation so we can ensure you r participation needs are met.   Brock University does not use AI Technology at any stage of the recruitment process.   We appreciate all applications received . C andidates that are selected for an interview will be contacted.   Learn more about Brock University by visiting www.brocku.ca ."
    }
  },
